: "thinking"}, {"text": "- **Deficit-Named Disorders as SpecificDisease:** IF a nominal phrase has a **deficit-state head** (a generic noun denoting lack or reduced function, such as a \"deficiency\" or \"deficient activity\" noun) that takes a prepositional or modifier **complement naming a biomolecular entity** (an enzyme, protein, or gene symbol), AND the surrounding context presents the phrase as a condition of an organism or population (for example, as a cause, an inherited or recessive trait, a prevalence, or a named clinical entity), THEN tag the full head-plus-complement span as **SpecificDisease**, including a parenthetical abbreviation that directly follows the complement. Do not tag only the enzyme or gene portion.\n  - **Negative constraint:** Do NOT apply this rule when (a) the biomolecular name appears without a deficit-state head; (b) the deficit construction reports an experimental or assay measurement (e.g., \"reduced activity was measured in vitro\") rather than a condition of an organism; (c) the phrase is a single symptom or sign with no deficit-state construction; or (d) the phrase denotes a broad class of conditions rather than one specific condition, which belongs to DiseaseClass. Phrases whose head is already a disease-category or eponymous term are outside this rule's scope and follow the standard SpecificDisease convention.", "type": "text"}], "diagnostics": null, "model": "claude-haiku-5-5", "role": "assistant", "stop_details": null, "stop_reason": "end_turn", "stop_sequence": null, "type": "message", "usage": {"cache_creation": {"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0}, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 0, "cache_read_input_tokens": 0, "inference_geo": "global", "input_tokens": 2386, "output_tokens": 2685, "output_tokens_details": {"thinking_tokens": 2231}, "service_tier": "batch", "speed": "standard"}}}